id: stable-foe
name: Stable Foe
type: awakening
subtype: greater
origin: mind
racial: Any
# An Adversary Transformation (dbu-rpg.com/adversary-transformations/). Said, not enforced, like every Prerequisite.
prerequisites: This character is an Adversary
tier: 1+
maxStacks: 1
aspects: 
bonuses: AG +2, TE +2
description: >
  This Antagonist can adapt to most threats put out by the heroes, at least until they’re on their last legs.
text: >
  Racial Requirement: Any / Transformation Type: Awakening / Awakening Type: Greater / Awakening Origin: Mind / Prerequisite(s): This character is an Adversary / Maximum No of Stacks: 1 / Tier of Power Requirement. 1+
  AG +2 · FO – · TE +2 · SC – · IN – · MA – · PE –

  Adaptive Antagonist: This Antagonist can adapt to most threats put out by the heroes, at least until they’re on their last legs.
  (1)-[Passive]: While above the Injured Health Threshold, increase your Combat Rolls and Soak Value by 1(T).
  (2)-[Passive]: Increase the Wound Rolls of your Attacking Maneuvers made through the Exploit Maneuver by 2(T).
  (3)-[Passive]: While below the Injured Health Threshold, increase your Surgency by 2(T).
  (4)-[Passive]: You gain access to the Directional Defense Villainous Maneuver.
  (5)-[1/Round, PCC/Encounter]: While below the Injured Health Threshold, you may use a Healing Surge as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.
  (6)-[Triggered/Start of Turn]: You may spend any number of Adversary Actions to remove an equal number of Combat Conditions (except Suffocating or Pinned). For the sake of this effect, if a Combat Condition has multiple stacks, each stack is considered its own Combat Condition for the amount of Adversary Actions required to remove it.
  (7)-[Triggered/Start of Combat Round]: You may spend an Adversary Action to use the Directional Defense Villainous Maneuver as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.

---

# Its own effects are its Traits' (traits/); its numbers are read from the header above (transformations.mjs).
